Description: This is a modified version of Battenberg v3.0.0. 
  Changes include processing chromosomes as p and q arms independently, 
  adjustments for INDEL handling, and other experimental updates. 
  This package is intended for experimental use only and should not 
  replace the official Battenberg release. To enable BEAGLE5 to run efficiently on low-memory nodes (e.g., 8 GB), 
  chromosomes are split into p and q arms and processed independently. 
  Java memory should be set to 5 GB. This setup requires additional checks 
  because some chromosomes may lack contributions from either the p or q arm 
  and also necessitates garbage collection. Furthermore, for Nextflow, parallel 
  workers need extra information to perform their tasks properly, so the 
  workflow has been updated accordingly.
